post("WIP-10", "wip", "static",
     "We shipped the frame viewer. Here is why.",
     "Because everyone kept telling us the frame was ‘too slim’ and then buying the one that was too chunky.\n\nThe frame viewer shows exactly how much glass you are giving away, in millimetres, from every angle, before anyone commits to a single number.\n\nIt is not a marketing feature. It is a way of stopping an argument in the office with a drawing instead of a debate.",
     "Photorealistic dark-mode software interface floating at an angle showing a 3D window model with a sightline dimension being adjusted, a light shining through the glass, clean and modern, neutral studio background, product lighting",
     "screen-mock", "wip", cta="Frame viewer, live. fenora.pro")

post("WIP-11", "wip", "static",
     "Six hundred emails a day that were not emails.",
     "Before this existed, this job lived in an inbox. A survey went in. A quote went out. A variation came back. A drawing got emailed. A cut list got retyped.\n\nNothing was wrong with any of those emails individually. The problem was that the job did not exist anywhere except as a chain of messages between six people, none of whom could see the whole thing.\n\nNow the job exists. The emails are just notifications.",
     "Photorealistic still life of an office desk buried in printed emails and job sheets, a laptop in the background showing a calm clean interface, a coffee cup, late light, before-and-after energy, warm",
     "screen-mock", "wip")

post("WIP-12", "wip", "carousel",
     "Materials: three systems, one quote",
     "Slide 1: TIMBER. Redwood, Accoya, sapele, oak, merenti. Box or spiral frame widths and depths. Cill projection, horns, arch profiles. Priced from section, species and glass — not from a square-metre figure.\n\nSlide 2: ALUMINIUM. Thermally broken with polyamide break. Sightlines drawn to the millimetre so the glass area is honest. Powder coat in and out, including dual colour.\n\nSlide 3: uPVC. Chamber count, reinforcement, welded or mechanically jointed. Chamfered or sculptured beading. Priced against your fabricator’s actual profile rates.\n\nSlide 4: All three, on the same quote, each drawn in its own terms.",
     "Photorealistic display of three window samples — timber, anthracite aluminium and white uPVC — arranged side by side on a dark surface under studio lighting, each with a different profile cross-section, premium and precise",
     "photo-real", "wip", cta="Timber, aluminium and uPVC. One configurator. fenora.pro")

post("WIP-13", "wip", "static",
     "Every unit, one line, everywhere.",
     "Frame. Section. Glass. Bars. Cill. Horns. Ironmongery. Finish in. Finish out. Fixings. Sealant.\n\nThat is the specification, and it is set on the unit — not on a job, not on a customer, not in an email — and then it is carried, unchanged, into the quotation, the survey, the workshop paperwork and the delivery note.\n\nThe same ten facts. Every time. Everywhere. Unchanged.\n\nThat is not a feature. That is the entire concept.",
     "Photorealistic extreme close-up of a window frame corner section on a dark surface, internal and external finishes visible, tiny labels and markers, macro studio lighting, engineering beauty, precise",
     "photo-real", "wip", cta="Specified once. Used everywhere. fenora.pro",
     li_lead="The whole architecture of this product is one sentence: specify once, carry everywhere. Everything else is detail.")

post("WIP-14", "wip", "reel",
     "Signed on the doorstep, not next month",
     "The quote is on a phone.\nThe customer reads the drawing. They read the specification. They sign.\n\nThe accepted specification becomes the order, and the order already has the drawing on it, and the drawing is the one the workshop will build from.\n\nThere is no gap between the thing they agreed to and the thing that gets made. In this industry, that gap is where the entire problem lives.",
     "Photorealistic 9:16 shot of a customer standing at their own front door signing on a phone, a tradesperson holding the door, warm afternoon light, new windows visible in the background of the hall, hopeful and human, portrait framing",
     "photo-trades", "wip", img="9:16", cta="Signed while the interest is there. fenora.pro")

