post("BP-04", "build-in-public", "static",
     "I did not start this to sell software.",
     "I started this because I have watched window companies lose money on jobs they had already won, and every single one of them could tell me exactly what happened, and every single one of them said the same sentence.\n\n“It was just a system thing.”\n\nIt is never a system thing. It is a survey that never reached the workshop, a quote that never reached the office, a variation that reached nobody.\n\nIt is a systems thing. It is exactly and only a systems thing.",
     "Photorealistic portrait photograph of a person working alone at a desk late in the evening, laptop glow, workshop or garage space, a stack of printed drawings, quiet and committed, documentary, muted",
     "photo-real", "build", cta="fenora.pro")

post("BP-05", "build-in-public", "static",
     "The bug that made me rebuild the survey app",
     "It did not lose data. That was never the problem.\n\nThe problem was that it worked, and it was easy, and it made me happy, and it was wrong — because it let a surveyor complete a job and call it done while a variation sat unresolved three screens away.\n\nThe app was making a decision that was not the app’s to make.\n\nThat took four months to rebuild and it is the single best change we have made.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a whiteboard covered in a chaotic diagram of user flows being redrawn, sticky notes, marker, a laptop with a debugger open, late night, engineering frustration, warm desk light",
     "screen-mock", "build")

post("BP-06", "build-in-public", "static",
     "Published pricing is a positioning decision",
     "There is a way to sell software that involves a discovery call, a needs analysis, a proposal, a negotiation and a four-month evaluation.\n\nAnd there is a way to publish the price and let people buy it.\n\nMost businesses in this trade do not have the luxury of the second option because they do not believe their price is defensible. Every one of them is wrong, and the ones who fix it win back three months of pipeline in a fortnight.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a simple printed price sheet pinned to a workshop wall next to a whiteboard of jobs, morning light, plain and confident, documentary, no branding",
     "photo-real", "build", cta="fenora.pro/pricing",
     li_lead="Publishing your price is not a discount strategy. It is a positioning strategy. It tells the market you are confident in what you built.")

post("BP-07", "build-in-public", "reel",
     "What 100 surveys taught me about UK houses",
     "After a hundred surveys I can tell you these things with confidence:\n\nThe drawing is wrong more often than it is right.\nThe reveal is square about a third of the time.\nThe lintel is a problem roughly half the time.\nNobody has ever had the cavity filled correctly.\nAt least one window per job is above a downpipe.\nThe customer is right about the wall being level about four per cent of the time.",
     "Photorealistic 9:16 shot of a stack of completed survey sheets on a desk beside a laser measure and a battered clipboard, a hand turning one over, morning light, documentary and warm, portrait framing",
     "photo-real", "build", img="9:16")

post("BP-08", "build-in-public", "static",
     "The complaint we will never be able to fix",
     "There is a guy. He emails us twice a month.\n\nHe does not like the interface. He does not want it in the cloud. He thinks the whole industry should be run from a spreadsheet and he is not entirely wrong.\n\nHe has been in window supply for thirty-one years and he has outlasted four different systems and he will probably outlast us.\n\nI answer both emails. Every time. He is right about about a third of it and that is a better ratio than most customers.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a laptop in a workshop with two email tabs open, a printed order from a window supplier on the desk, an old rule and a pencil, warm and wry, documentary",
     "photo-real", "build")

post("BP-09", "build-in-public", "static",
     "What “full stack” actually means for a window business",
     "Not a tech stack. A business stack.\n\nCRM. Planning search. Survey app. Configurator. Quoting. Production. Tasks. Teams. Delivery. Invoicing.\n\nOne record that carries the specification, the price, the evidence and the history from enquiry to final payment.\n\nIf any one of those is a separate system with a separate login, somebody in your business is retyping something today. Somebody is always retyping something.",
     "Photorealistic dark-mode software interface floating at an angle showing a modular grid of connected workflow stages, warm accent colours, clean and modern, neutral background, cinematic product lighting",
     "screen-mock", "build", cta="Find the thing you are retyping. fenora.pro")

post("BP-10", "build-in-public", "carousel",
     "Build log, quarter by quarter",
     "This quarter:\n\nShipped: offline survey sync. Frame viewer. Revision quotes with a clean diff.\n\nFixed: a margin bug that only triggered on Rev 2 quotes, and has been quietly annoying since launch.\n\nRefused: a dashboard with fourteen tiles. It was beautiful. It was useless.\n\nLearned: every single feature request in this trade is either “make it faster” or “stop losing my information”. That is the entire product. That is it.",
     "Photorealistic overhead photograph of a build-in-public style quarterly planning board: a grid, sticky notes, a marker, a coffee ring, a printed screenshot, a laptop edge, warm desk light, honest and scrappy",
     "screen-mock", "build", cta="Ship notes, in the open. fenora.pro")

post("BP-11", "build-in-public", "static",
     "“Can we just…” is the most important sentence in product.",
     "“Can we just put the survey on the phone?”\n\n“Can we just have the quote come out with the drawing on it?”\n\n“Can we just make the delivery wait until the balance is paid?”\n\n“Can we just not retype the sizes?”\n\nEvery single good decision in this product came from a version of that sentence spoken by somebody in the trade who was annoyed on a Tuesday.\n\nWe are not designing software here. We are taking notes.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a notepad on a workshop bench with a short handwritten list, a biro, a phone with a voice memo recording indicator, coffee, workshop light, intimate and documentary",
     "photo-real", "build", cta="fenora.pro")

post("BP-12", "build-in-public", "static",
     "We are hiring. Here is the honest version.",
     "We are looking for someone who has actually stood in a reveal.\n\nNot a developer with a nice story about the trades. Someone who can look at a survey photo and say “that lintel is doing nothing, that cavity is full, and that trickle vent is in the wrong place” and then describe it in a sentence that a software developer can build from.\n\nThat person is worth more than another senior developer and they are much harder to find.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a small team working together at a long table in a workshop, a large monitor showing a window model, samples of timber and profiles on the table, warm collaborative light, candid and real",
     "photo-real", "build")


