post("TM-01", "team", "reel",
     "POV: you open the survey app and the quoted sizes are already there",
     "Opening by opening, the quoted size and the full specification are already on the phone.\n\nThe survey sheet. The glazing. The bar type. The ironmongery. The cill projection. All of it.\n\nSo the survey stops being a data entry job and starts being a verification job. You are checking, not collecting.\n\nAnd for the first time, the person on site and the person in the office are looking at the same job.",
     "Photorealistic 9:16 shot of a surveyor on a site holding a phone showing a detailed opening list, expression of relief, morning light in a half-stripped UK room, warm and human, portrait framing",
     "photo-trades", "team", img="9:16", cta="fenora.pro")

post("TM-02", "team", "static",
     "The office is not a back office.",
     "The office is where the job is won or lost for reasons the fitter will never see.\n\nThe office is the quote that goes out in eleven minutes instead of two days. The office is the drawing that is attached. The office is the variation that gets priced on the same day it is flagged. The office is the deposit letter that goes out automatically.\n\nThe office is the whole business and it is usually the quietest room in it.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a small trade office: two people, a good desk, a window sample, a monitor showing a quote, morning light, calm and competent, not frantic, documentary business photography",
     "photo-real", "team")

post("TM-03", "team", "static",
     "The workshop is not a factory. It is a conversation.",
     "The workshop does not need a salesperson. The workshop needs the drawing, the cut list, the label, the schedule and the finish schedule, all correct, in that order, on the day.\n\nGive a workshop those five things and it will run at 95% first-time-right without a single phone call.\n\nThen take the phone away and give the sales team their morning back.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a skilled joiner at a workbench in a UK workshop, a printed cut list and label beside him, timber and finished window frames in the background, sawdust in a shaft of light, warm and skilled, documentary",
     "photo-trades", "team", cta="The spec that priced the quote produces the purchase order, the cut list, the labels and the drawings. fenora.pro")

post("TM-04", "team", "reel",
     "The most underrated person in a window business",
     "Not the fitter. Not the salesperson. Not even the office.\n\nThe person who orders the glass and is right about the lead time.\n\nThat person knows that 24mm with a warm edge is nine days and 24mm standard is four. That person knows the uPVC is on holiday in August. That person knows to order the ironmongery before the frame arrives and not after.\n\nThat person is usually called Steve and is currently on a break.",
     "Photorealistic 9:16 shot of a person at a desk surrounded by glass samples, a supplier catalogue and a phone, looking calm and knowledgeable, a coffee going cold, warm office light, quietly authoritative, portrait framing",
     "photo-real", "team", img="9:16")

post("TM-05", "team", "static",
     "The apprentice. Feed him properly.",
     "The best thing you can do for an apprentice is to make him record the job properly.\n\nNot the fitting. The job. The survey, the photos, the variations, the numbers, the materials. All of it, on a system, as he goes.\n\nIn three years he will not be an apprentice. He will be running jobs, pricing them properly, and not losing the information that everyone else loses.\n\nAnd in five years you will have a manager, and you will not have had to train one.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a young apprentice tradesperson kneeling at a window opening with a phone photographing the details, a laser measure and notebook, wearing clean new workwear, focused, morning light, hopeful and warm",
     "photo-trades", "team")

post("TM-06", "team", "static",
     "Subcontractors need the same system, not more WhatsApp.",
     "A subcontract fitter who has to chase you for a drawing is a subcontract fitter who will do it slightly differently, on a slightly different day, and you will not find out until the customer mentions it.\n\nGive them the job. Not a PDF of a job.\n\nThey see the same opening-by-opening record you see. Same sizes, same spec, same evidence, same conditions. They are part of the job, so the job should include them.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of two tradespeople from different vans working together on a window installation, one passing a frame, a shared job sheet on a clipboard between them, overcast daylight, partnership energy, documentary",
     "photo-trades", "team", cta="Office, surveyors, fitters and subs on the same job. fenora.pro")

post("TM-07", "team", "static",
     "Seven systems, one person keeping them in step. Sound familiar?",
     "The CRM knows nothing about windows.\nThe spreadsheet is priced by one person.\nThe survey app cannot see the quote.\nThe quoting software cannot see the survey.\nThe decisions live in WhatsApp.\nThe dates live in a calendar.\nThe delivery has no job attached.\n\nOne job, entered six times, each slightly different. Somebody is a person in the middle keeping them in step. You know who. So do they.",
     "Photorealistic photograph of a single UK tradesperson looking slightly overwhelmed, surrounded by a laptop, a clipboard, a phone, a paper file, a delivery note and a wall calendar, muted and relatable, documentary",
     "photo-real", "team", cta="One record that travels the whole way through the business. fenora.pro")

